eople aren't aware of  uh where they're trying to essentially  stop the bleeding maybe or at least  address the problem  now again two really important points so  one is is the rebalancing the good ones  right the swenson acolytes etc you know  rest in peace david um they do rebalance  and and that was something that  i was always really proud of the way we  did that at carolina and at notre dame  is is we're very active rebounds because  when you're in the endowment business or  the pension business you're not in the  get-rich business  concentration makes you rich  diversification keeps you rich and  rebalancing keeps you richer  because you're constantly buying cheap  and selling deer  um all great fortunes in the world came  from concentration  how do you create a small fortune start  with a large fortune and stay  concentrated so there will always be  cycles and if you can hold forever right  in a tax-deferred structure like  berkshire you should do that but you  should lever up that's what they do but  most people  uh should just constantly rebalance with  a good plan they should have some  get-rich money i would say you should  have three buckets liquidity bucket to  fund your lifestyle a get-rich-bucket to  do all the fun stuff the friends condo  deal the brother-in-law's venture you're  gonna lose at all anyway so just make it  small and then stay rich bucket  diversify that and these institutions  are looking at that storage bucket and  saying okay my equities just fell a lot  my tech equities fell more let's go buy  some stuff that's on sale maybe buy some  chinese equities maybe buy some of these  these cloud companies although i think  the cloud companies are still too  expensive  um  then on the flip side they're looking at  their private port and here's the one  problem  the very best of the very best  the yales the notre dames the you know  unc's etc the very best of the very best  in performance they have this lag  problem  the public markets adjust immediately  and then you have a denominator problem  because your private markets don't  adjust and so you have a denominator  problem and that your total fund value  went down so your weighting in private  went up but you can't really sell unless  you sell in the secondary market and  you're going to take a massive haircut  because there's very little liquidity so  doing that doesn't make any sense so you  have to actually talk to your el to your  gps and say well how far are valuations  actually going to fall because they're  going to fall  but they'll be sticky down instead of  immediate because in private it's the  escalator up  i mean in public is the escalator up in  the elevator down  right in the private world it's the  escalator up and the escalator down it  just takes longer to come down

